//! run
//! signal: ABRT
//! stderr: runtime error: division by zero
//! stdout:
//| before
// A failed runtime check prints its message and calls `abort` (D11.4), so the
// program dies by SIGABRT. The `signal: ABRT` directive above is the long
// spelling of the `abort` one (toolchain.md 7.3), and this test is deliberately
// run/errors/006_division_by_zero.ft with the other spelling: it is the only
// end-to-end proof that the two agree, so neither file is redundant and
// deleting either one loses that. Its `stderr:` substring is looked for after
// qemu-user's own notice about the signal is dropped.
fn zero() i32 {
    return 0;
}

fn main() i32 {
    i32 d = zero();
    println("before");
    println(7 / d);
    return 0;
}
